<section class="section reveal" id="stakeholder-alignment">
  <span class="section-label">Strategy</span>
  <h2>Navigating Stakeholder Tensions</h2>

  <p>AI products exist at the intersection of competing interests: executives want ROI, engineers want technical rigor, compliance wants risk management, and users want solutions that work. The architect must navigate these tensions transparently.</p>

  <p>Alignment is not consensus—it is shared understanding of tradeoffs and explicit agreement on which constraints matter most. The architect's role is to make these decisions visible.</p>

