  <h3>Building Alignment Through Transparent Tradeoffs</h3>
  <p>The most effective alignment tool is shared understanding. When every stakeholder knows why a decision was made and what constraints were balanced, they become allies instead of obstacles. Document your tradeoff decisions explicitly.</p>

  <div class="key-takeaway">
    <h4>✦ Key Takeaways</h4>
    <ul>
      <li>Stakeholder alignment is shared understanding of tradeoffs, not perfect agreement</li>
      <li>Every stakeholder perspective is valid within their domain</li>
      <li>The architect translates between technical and business language</li>
      <li>Explicit tradeoff discussions prevent misalignment later</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>

