<section class="section reveal" id="rapid-iteration">
  <span class="section-label">Practice</span>
  <h2>Prototyping and Iterative Validation</h2>

  <p>Design thinking is built on rapid iteration: prototype quickly, test with users, learn, and repeat. For AI systems, start with simple baselines—rules, heuristics, or manual processes—that test the core hypothesis before investing in ML complexity.</p>

  <p>The fastest way to validate an AI concept is to build the smallest system that tests the fundamental assumption. This might not use ML at all.</p>

  <div class="code-header"><span class="code-lang">Python</span><button class="copy-btn">Copy</button></div>
  <pre><code><span class="cm"># Iteration 0: Rule-based baseline</span>
<span class="kw">def</span> <span class="fn">recommend_v0</span>(<span class="va">query</span>):
    <span class="kw">if</span> <span class="st">"billing"</span> <span class="kw">in</span> <span class="va">query</span>:
        <span class="kw">return</span> [<span class="st">"billing_faq.md"</span>]

<span class="cm"># Iteration 1: TF-IDF</span>
<span class="kw">def</span> <span class="fn">recommend_v1</span>(<span class="va">query</span>):
    <span class="va">scores</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="fn">tfidf</span>(<span class="va">query</span>, <span class="va">articles</span>)
    <span class="kw">return</span> <span class="fn">top_k</span>(<span class="va">scores</span>, <span class="nm">5</span>)

<span class="cm"># Iteration 2: Embeddings</span>
<span class="kw">def</span> <span class="fn">recommend_v2</span>(<span class="va">query</span>):
    <span class="va">q_embed</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="fn">embed</span>(<span class="va">query</span>)
    <span class="va">scores</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="fn">cosine_sim</span>(<span class="va">q_embed</span>, <span class="va">embeds</span>)
    <span class="kw">return</span> <span class="fn">top_k</span>(<span class="va">scores</span>, <span class="nm">5</span>)</code></pre>
  <div class="code-explain">
    <p><strong>The iteration strategy:</strong> Start simple. Each iteration adds capability only if the previous version proves the core hypothesis. Do not add ML complexity until basic value is demonstrated.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="key-takeaway">
    <h4>✦ Key Takeaways</h4>
    <ul>
      <li>Start simple: rules, heuristics, or manual processes validate core hypotheses</li>
      <li>Iterate on product metrics first, then optimize model metrics</li>
      <li>Fail fast: if simple approaches don't drive adoption, ML complexity won't either</li>
      <li>Test with real users at each iteration, not just final validation</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>

